  "docText": [
    "SOLAR®",
    "Biamp Design System",
    "1.0",
    "Checkbox",
    "Description",
    "Multi-select box for independent choices. Use when the user can pick zero, one, or many from a set (terms, filter facets, select-all-rows). For a single on/off setting, use Toggle. For exclusive one-of-many, use Radio. Commit on click.",
    "States",
    "checked=false / checked=true — the two base states.\nmixed=true — indeterminate dash, used on a parent when some children are checked.\nhover=true — transient background on the hit area.\nfocus=true — the shared shadow/focus/default effect style plus a border/feedback/focus/strong stroke, so the ring reads at 16px.\ndisabled=true — locked value, not-allowed cursor.\nThere is no pressed state. 12 variants in total.",
    "Content",
    "Pair with a visible label to the right (\"I agree to the terms\"). The full label is the click target — users should not have to hit the 16px box. Max label width stays within a comfortable reading measure (<75ch). Group related checkboxes with a fieldset + legend pattern.",
    "Accessibility",
    "Render as <input type=\"checkbox\">. Label via <label for=\"\"> — clicking the label toggles. aria-checked reflects true/false/mixed. Keyboard: Space toggles; Tab moves focus. Focus ring wraps the full label + box so it's visible even when the box is tiny.",
    "Rules",
    "Do\n\n• Make the full label clickable — not just the box\n• Use mixed on parents when some children are checked\n• Group related checkboxes in a fieldset\n• Commit on click, no confirm step",
    "Don't\n\n• Don't use for single on/off — that's Toggle\n• Don't use for exclusive choice — that's Radio\n• Don't make the 16px box the only click target\n• Don't rely on color alone for checked state — show the tick"
  ],
  "pageContext": null
